  "body": "## What changed\n\n- **`vertex`** — full Google Vertex AI adapter: renewable Application Default Credentials (ADC) via `google-auth`, native `publisherModels` paginated discovery, endpoint composition. New `providers/vertex/` + `providers/google_openai/` subpackages.\n- **`openai`** — OpenAI/ChatGPT connected account, reusing our existing `chatgpt_oauth` provider under a second catalog id (both route to `_create_chatgpt_oauth`).\n- **Dependency bump**: `openai` 2.44.0 → **2.54.0** (capped `<3` to stay off the HTTPX2 3.x line that would ripple through our whole httpx-based provider layer), plus `google-auth[requests]` + `requests[socks]`. Resolved versions match upstream's lock exactly.\n- `ProviderDescriptor` gains `configuration_attrs()`/`required_settings_attrs` so ADC providers (no credential env) report configured correctly in admin status.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Full suite: **3969 passed / 6 failed** (6 = pre-existing PowerShell-installer baseline).\n- `ruff format --check`, `ruff check`, `ty check`: clean.\n- Fixed an import-boundary regression (google_openai now imports from the `openai_chat` facade, not submodules) and a test typing mismatch.\n\n## Notes / residual risks\n\n- `openai` is an **alias** of `chatgpt_oauth`, not a byte-for-byte port of upstream's separate `openai_codex` adapter — same OAuth + Responses protocol, but keep our `CHATGPT_OAUTH_*` credential env.\n- `vertex` has no live round-trip (ADC + a GCP project required); auth, discovery, and request construction are unit-tested.\n- The openai SDK `<3` cap is deliberate: 3.0.0's HTTPX2 migration is a breaking transport change; revisit when the fork migrates off `httpx` entirely.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
