    "message": "feat(providers): add Google Vertex AI + OpenAI connected account\n\n- vertex: full Google Vertex AI adapter (renewable Application Default Credentials\n  auth via google-auth, native publisherModels paginated discovery, endpoint\n  composition). New providers/vertex/ + providers/google_openai/ subpackages.\n- openai: OpenAI/ChatGPT connected account, reusing our existing chatgpt_oauth\n  provider under a second catalog id (both route to _create_chatgpt_oauth).\n- Dependency bump: openai 2.44.0 -> 2.54.0 (<3, to stay off the HTTPX2 3.x line),\n  + google-auth[requests] + requests[socks]. Matches upstream's lock exactly.\n- ProviderDescriptor gains configuration_attrs()/required_settings_attrs so ADC\n  providers (no credential env) report configured correctly in admin status.\n\nVerification: full suite 3969 passed / 6 pre-existing PS-installer failures\n(baseline unchanged); ruff format/check + ty clean. Fixed an import-boundary\nregression (google_openai imported openai_chat submodules instead of the facade)\nand a test typing mismatch (bare async fn vs GoogleAccessTokenProvider).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
